    "done_when": "The coil-edit regeneration certificate row runs once through _certificate_rows_as_processes in ONE H200 job (betelgeuse, reservation gpu_0003_grpA, one card, 8 CPUs, an explicit --mem, TMPDIR=/tmp in submit and payload, the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python without uv, submitted with RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 sbatch, which is a separate job on the H200 node and not a step of the fleet allocation the HOST line describes, and is authorised; never srun or salloc. Submit for real and read squeue after a minute; only if it is still PENDING on a resource or configuration reason resubmit to titan (--partition=titan --gres=gpu:1) and say so; CPU in place on the fleet node is the last rung and its walls are not the GPU measurement, --mem=64G, --time=00:45:00). Its per-row receipt is persisted under docs/figures/cpu-compile-abort/coil-edit-regeneration-row/ with a receipt-relative state path and both exit fields (if the earlier certificate rows live elsewhere, name that location in the report rather than writing there), and records whether it completes, its mapping count at program load, and its solve wall separated from compile wall. A row that fails is recorded as measured. The report /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/cca-coil-edit-regeneration-row.md quotes the receipt fields by JSON path. If the job outlasts your turn, commit, write status waiting with the sacct probe as wait_probe and the job id in wait_condition, and end the turn; the recovery sweep resumes you when the job is terminal. Keep scratch under the run directory, not /tmp, which is at 91 percent on the fleet node; a baseline arm extracts only the subtrees it imports and removes them before the manifest. This gate measures only this node; a failure outside its scope goes under follow_ons.",
